## Per-call attributes

The `weave.attributes()` context manager lets you add metadata to specific traced operations. Use it to tag particular function calls or evaluation runs with contextual information.

> [!TIP]
>
> You can't modify `call.attributes` once the call starts. Use this
> context manager to set any metadata before invoking the op.

**Python**

```python lines theme={"system"}
import weave

weave.init("[TEAM-NAME]/[PROJECT-NAME]")

@weave.op
def my_function(name: str):
    return f"Hello, {name}!"

# Add attributes to a specific call
with weave.attributes({'env': 'production', 'user_id': '12345'}):
    result = my_function("World")
```

